  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What onboarding actually indexes",
      "items": [
        "chunkProfile reads one profile row, never the chat archive",
        "Only 4 shapes are embedded: one chunk per service, one meta chunk, one chunk per conversation_example, or raw paragraphs when no structured JSON exists",
        "selectBestExamples caps the uploaded chat at 14 pairs across 6 categories before embedding"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Gap versus Dify",
      "items": [
        "inbox_messages is a write-only archive: no code path embeds a real customer conversation",
        "Feedback corrections from send mutate profiles but never call upsertKnowledgeChunks, so the vector store stays stale until the owner re-saves Settings",
        "Retrieval is vector-only at a fixed 0.3 threshold: no hybrid keyword search, no rerank stage, no metadata filter, no retrieval test surface"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Ingest mechanics",
      "items": [
        "Both writes re-embed the whole set, then delete-all-then-insert",
        "Fire-and-forget: re-index failures are logged only, never surfaced to the owner",
        "RLS scopes rows by user_id, and the SQL match function filters on the same column"
      ]
    }
  ]
